From 768dde6a76be9d43419a92d0db4fb449842f3cad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:49:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/43] fix(refinery): Engineer.LoadConfig reads
 settings/config.json, not rig-root (gfork-hgx)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Engineer.LoadConfig read <rig>/config.json (rig root), but the canonical
merge_queue config operators write via `gt rig settings set` lives at
<rig>/settings/config.json (config.RigSettingsPath). Every rig on disk has an
empty root config.json and the real config under settings/, so LoadConfig
silently returned defaults and ignored require_review, gates, merge_strategy,
etc.

No live impact today — the Go merge engine (LoadConfig/doMergePR/ProcessMRInfo)
has zero non-test callers; the live refinery is the mol-refinery-patrol LLM
formula merging via `gh pr merge`, and its require_review comes from template
vars that already read settings/config.json. This is a latent landmine: the day
Engineer.Process is wired into a runtime path it would read the wrong file.

Fix (matches unmerged upstream PR #4432): read config.RigSettingsPath(e.rig.Path).
Tests redirected to write settings/config.json via a new writeEngineerSettingsConfig
helper (mirrors #4432's helper). go test -race ./internal/refinery: all LoadConfig
tests pass. Pre-existing TestEngineerClearAgentActiveMRUsesTownBeadsDir failure
(BEADS_DIR/bd-subprocess env class) verified identical with this change stashed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
